From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: toolbar drop targets, bounding size, standard bitmap replacement

TBSTYLE_REGISTERDROP, TB_SETBOUNDINGSIZE, TB_REPLACEBITMAP of standard
bitmaps and of other modules' bitmaps, the tooltip of a button whose
command changes (TB_SETCMDID), combined custom draw answers to the erase
and TBIMHT_BACKGROUND in TB_SETINSERTMARK were FIXMEs.

- TBSTYLE_REGISTERDROP: the toolbar registers itself as a drop target
  (when OLE is initialized); over a button it asks the parent for that
  button's drop target (TBN_GETOBJECT, IID_IDropTarget) and hands it the
  drag -- enter, over, leave when it moves to another button, drop.
- TB_SETBOUNDINGSIZE: a wrapping toolbar wraps its rows at the bounding
  width.
- TB_REPLACEBITMAP: standard bitmaps (HINST_COMMCTRL) are found and
  replaced like any other, from any module; the default image list is
  made again from the bitmaps, in their order (it lost its place
  before).
- TB_SETCMDID moves the button's tooltip tool to the new command.
- WM_ERASEBKGND: custom draw answers combine (CDRF_SKIPDEFAULT with
  CDRF_NOTIFYPOSTERASE skips the erase); TB_SETINSERTMARK accepts
  TBIMHT_BACKGROUND; a separator of a toolbar that is not flat is empty
  space, as on Windows.

Wine's comctl32 toolbar tests: 2107 tests, no failures, as before.

Gate: test/toolbar2-gate.sh (Xvfb, test/toolbar2-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_DROP_OBJECT, SG_MUTANT_NO_BOUNDING
(comctl32/toolbar.c).
